      "text": "Since $x^{2017} - 2x + 1 = 0,$ then \\[x^{2017} = 2x - 1.\\]Using this result, we can compute \\[\\begin{aligned} x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1 &= x^{2017} - 1 \\\\ &= (2x - 1) - 1 \\\\ &= 2x - 2 \\\\ &= \\boxed{2}.\\end{aligned}.\\]Comment place here.\n\n1. We are given the equation \\( x^{2017} - 2x + 1 = 0 \\) and need to find the value of \\( x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1 \\).\n\n2. Start by rearranging the given equation:\n   \\[\n   x^{2017} = 2x - 1\n   \\]\n\n3. Notice that if we manipulate the expression \\( x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1 \\) in a specific way, we can use the given equation to simplify it. Consider the sum:\n   \\[\n   S = x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1\n   \\]\n\n4. The sum \\( S \\) is a geometric series with the first term \\( a = 1 \\) and common ratio \\( r = x \\). The number of terms is \\( 2017 \\). The sum of a geometric series is given by:\n   \\[\n   S = \\frac{a(1 - r^n)}{1 - r}\n   \\]\n   where \\( n \\) is the number of terms.\n\n5. Substitute \\( a = 1 \\), \\( r = x \\), and \\( n = 2017 \\) into the formula:\n   \\[\n   S = \\frac{1(1 - x^{2017})}{1 - x}\n   \\]\n\n6. From the given equation, we know \\( x^{2017} = 2x - 1 \\). Substitute \\( x^{2017} \\) into the expression:\n   \\[\n   S = \\frac{1(1 - (2x - 1))}{1 - x} = \\frac{1 + 1 - 2x}{1 - x} = \\frac{2 - 2x}{1 - x}\n   \\]\n\n7. Simplify the fraction:\n   \\[\n   S = \\frac{2(1 - x)}{1 - x} = 2\n   \\]\n\nThe final answer is \\(\\boxed{2}\\).",
