      "text": "Since $x^{2017} - 2x + 1 = 0,$ we can rewrite it as $x^{2017} = 2x - 1.$\nWe want to find the value of $x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1,$ which is the sum of the geometric series with first term $x$ and common ratio $x.$\nThe sum of a geometric series is given by $\\frac{a(1 - r^n)}{1 - r},$ where $a$ is the first term, $r$ is the common ratio, and $n$ is the number of terms.\nIn this case, $a = x,$ $r = x,$ and $n = 2016,$ so we can write the sum as\n\\[x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1 = \\frac{x(1 - x^{2016})}{1 - x}.\\]\nSince $x^{2017} = 2x - 1,$ we have $x^{2016} = \\frac{2x - 1}{x}.$\nSubstituting this into the expression above, we get\n\\[x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1 = \\frac{x\\left(1 - \\left(\\frac{2x - 1}{x}\\right)^{2016}\\right)}{1 - x}.\\]\nSimplifying the numerator, we have\n\\[x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1 = \\frac{x\\left(1 - \\frac{(2x - 1)^{2016}}{x^{2016}}\\right)}{1 - x} = \\frac{x\\left(\\frac{x^{2016} - (2x - 1)^{2016}}{x^{2016}}\\right)}{1 - x}.\\]\nExpanding $(2x - 1)^{2016},$ we have\n\\[x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1 = \\frac{x(x^{2016} - (2x - 1)^{2016})}{x^{2016}(1 - x)} = \\frac{x^{2017} - (2x - 1)^{2016}}{x^{2016}(1 - x)}.\\]\nSince $x$ satisfies the equation $x^{2017} - 2x + 1 = 0,$ we have\n\\[x^{2017} - (2x - 1)^{2016} = 0 - (2x - 1)^{2016} = -(2x - 1)^{2016}.\\]\nSubstituting this into the expression above, we get\n\\begin{align*}\nx^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1 &= \\frac{-(2x - 1)^{2016}}{x^{2016}(1 - x)} \\\\\n&= \\frac{-x^{2016} + x^{2015}}{x^{2016}(1 - x)} \\\\\n&= \\frac{-x^{2015}(x - 1)}{x^{2016}(1 - x)} \\\\\n&= \\frac{-x(x - 1)}{x^{2016}(1 - x)} \\\\\n&= \\frac{-x}{x^{2015}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{-1}{x^{2014}}.\n\\end{align*}\nThus, the value of $x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1$ is $\\boxed{-1}.$\nThe answer is: -1",
