      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "Let $f(x) = x^{2017} - 2x + 1$.\nNote that $f(1) = 0$ and $f(-1) = 2 - 1 + 1 = 2 \\neq 0$.\nThus, by the IVT, there exists a $c \\in (-1, 1)$ such that $f(c) = 0$.\nLet $g(x) = x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1$.\nThen we have\n\\[g(x) = x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1 = f(x). \\tag*{}[/latex]\n\nI very much appreciate your feedback. It's thank to YGMama",
